<!doctype html>
<!--
  What the names mean.

  **The garden's ten areas each gather the plants of one theme, and a plant's
  name is what says which.** The head of the genus carries the theme, the ending
  of the genus carries which of the theme's three parts the words under the
  plant are drawn from, and the second word says the one way the plant most
  departs from its genus. None of that was written anywhere a reader could find
  it; it was in docs/NAMES-AND-THEMES.md, `Epithet.swift` and a comment in
  `Areas.swift`. This is the dictionary a reader looks it up in.

  **Drawn, not written out.** The entries and the glossary come from
  `meanings.js`, which the entry under every area's drawing is drawn from too,
  so the short account on an area page and the long one here are one table read
  twice. Each area page links to its own entry, `/meanings#waiting` and so on.
  Since 24 September every root and every second word has a drawing, so a
  reader can follow a name by its pictures in any language.

  Follows the reader's system, light or dark, as the other pages of words do.
  An area page is a night because it is lit by its own sky; this page has none.

  No `noindex`: it publishes no plant anybody grew, only the key to reading
  one, which is the reason `/g` and the areas carry it. Static, like the rest:
  no analytics, no font CDN, no third-party anything.
-->
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1, viewport-fit=cover" />
    <title>Peace Garden — what the names mean</title>
    <meta name="description" content="What brings a plant to each of the garden's ten areas, and what the two words of its name say about it." />
    <meta name="color-scheme" content="dark light" />
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/site.css" />
    <link rel="icon" href="/assets/icon.svg" type="image/svg+xml" />
    <link rel="apple-touch-icon" href="/assets/icon-180.png" />
  </head>

  <body>
    <div class="pool" aria-hidden="true"></div>

    <main class="page meanings-page" id="page">
      <!--
        The bar. On every page of the site, and the only way between any two of
        them that is not a link somebody happened to put in a paragraph.
        `site.css` §The bar says why it is the masthead with two things added
        rather than a header of its own.
      -->
      <header class="masthead bar">
        <a class="bar__home" href="/">
          <img class="mark" src="/assets/icon.svg" alt="" width="44" height="44" />
          <span class="wordmark">Peace Garden</span>
        </a>
        <!--
          The ways on from here, as glyphs rather than words, so they read the
          same in every language: the garden (the app's own Garden mark,
          `GardenGlyph` in Chrome.swift), what the names mean (an open book,
          the app's `MeaningsGlyph`), and the language. Each glyph's words
          are its name and tooltip, written from the catalogue by the page's
          script. See site.css §The bar's glyphs.
        -->
        <span class="bar__ways">
          <a class="bar-glyph" href="/garden" data-s-label="gardenTitle"><svg class="bar-glyph__mark" viewBox="0 0 15 15" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M 4.674 4.059 C 3.796 1.407, 6.716 1.407, 5.838 4.059 C 8.089 2.405, 8.991 5.181, 6.198 5.166 C 8.467 6.795, 6.105 8.512, 5.256 5.850 C 4.407 8.512, 2.045 6.795, 4.314 5.166 C 1.521 5.181, 2.423 2.405, 4.674 4.059 Z M 5.784 14.100 C 5.652 10.932, 5.124 9.612, 5.256 7.500 M 10.140 14.100 C 9.678 10.932, 9.150 8.556, 8.622 6.180 M 10.140 14.100 C 10.338 10.404, 10.470 6.972, 10.338 3.540 M 10.140 14.100 C 10.800 10.932, 11.658 8.820, 12.318 6.972 M 4.200 14.100 L 11.328 14.100" vector-effect="non-scaling-stroke" /></svg></a>
          <a class="bar-glyph" href="/meanings" data-s-label="meaningsTitle"><svg class="bar-glyph__mark" viewBox="0 0 20 20" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M10 5.2C8.2 3.9 5.4 3.5 2.75 3.9V15.4C5.4 15 8.2 15.4 10 16.7C11.8 15.4 14.6 15 17.25 15.4V3.9C14.6 3.5 11.8 3.9 10 5.2ZM10 5.2V16.7" vector-effect="non-scaling-stroke" /></svg></a>
          <label class="bar-language">
            <span class="visually-hidden" id="language-label"></span>
            <svg class="bar-language__mark" viewBox="0 0 20 20" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M3 10a7 7 0 1 0 14 0a7 7 0 1 0 -14 0M10 3C7.4 5.3 7.4 14.7 10 17M10 3C12.6 5.3 12.6 14.7 10 17M3 10H17M4.2 6.2H15.8M4.2 13.8H15.8" vector-effect="non-scaling-stroke" /></svg>
            <span class="chooser__field">
              <select id="language" class="chooser__select"></select>
              <svg class="chooser__mark" viewBox="0 0 16 16" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M4 6.5 L8 10.5 L12 6.5" /></svg>
            </span>
          </label>
        </span>
      </header>

      <h1 class="heading" data-s="meaningsTitle"></h1>
      <p class="body" data-s="meaningsAbout"></p>

      <!--
        One name, taken apart: each piece of it, and what that piece says. It
        is read back through `passages.js` by `meanings.js`, so it is filed by
        the same rule the passage under a real plant is.
      -->
      <figure class="meanings-example" id="example" hidden></figure>

      <!--
        The ten areas as the map's tiles, each a way to its entry below: a
        contents in pictures, named for a screen reader by the areas' own names.
      -->
      <nav class="meanings-index" id="index" hidden></nav>

      <!--
        The ten entries, set as a dictionary sets a word: the theme as the
        headword with its area's tile, the definition, the name-starts as the
        etymology with a drawing of each root, and the three parts as the
        numbered senses. A list because it is one, and each entry is the anchor
        its area page links to — `/meanings#waiting` and so on. See site.css
        §The page at /meanings.
      -->
      <ol class="lexicon" id="lexicon"></ol>

      <p class="body meanings-second" data-s="meaningsSecond"></p>

      <!-- The second words, each with a drawing of what it says. -->
      <dl class="glossary" id="epithets" hidden></dl>

      <!--
        The foot: one hairline and the privacy notice. The language it used to
        hold went up into the bar, beside the other ways on from a page.
      -->
      <footer class="foot bar-foot">
        <a class="bar-foot__link" href="/privacy" data-s="privacyTitle"></a>
      </footer>
    </main>

    <script type="module" src="/assets/js/plain.js"></script>
    <script type="module" src="/assets/js/meaningspage.js"></script>
  </body>
</html>
